{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe code-review `tests` overlay (blocking at 0.54 —\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json:110-121`) is selected only when a changed file\nmatches its `applies_to` globs `**/test_*.py`, `**/*_test.py`, `**/tests/**`\n(`registry.glob_triggered_overlays`, `registry.py:340-356`). A change adding product logic and\ntouching no test file never runs it unless the base reviewer happens to recommend it, and guard\n(vii) (`code-review-tests.md:97`) keeps a bare coverage-gap finding advisory.\n\nFour changes adding declarations merged on `LLM-Review +1` with zero test files: Gerrit 388\n(`d9e0f0e733`, 15 added `def`/`class` lines, new `git_adapter.py`), 1920 (`721cb7d6ac`, 3), 1737\n(`1c2bf6e57b`, 22), 1703 (`83d91d488c`, 8). 388 later produced three bugs\n(`79c6-eaf3-38af-4ce9` + two siblings) — the `git_adapter` by-path-load family the epic names.\nGerrit 1547 (`24917e843b`) is a NEGATIVE case: comment-only source delta, 0 added `def`/`class`.\nApproved in the 2026-08-21 fortnight defect review; diff-coverage was rejected — this project\ntests behaviour, not coverage %.\n\n## Approach\nFire the overlay from the diff CONTENT, where the diff and the changed files are both known.\n1. `content_triggered_overlays` (`registry.py:461`) takes `(diff_text, repo_root)` only and is\n   path-blind by construction (every helper skips the `+++`/`---` headers), so the \"changes no test\n   file\" half of the rule has no operand there today. Add a keyword-only\n   `changed_files: Sequence[str] = ()` — call sites stay positional — and pass the step's `changed`\n   list at `workflow_ops.py:99`.\n2. The detector is a NEW module-level helper (`_has_added_declaration`), NOT extra branches inside\n   `content_triggered_overlays`: `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` fails on `new>0` and\n   the baseline may not be raised. It fires when, for some changed file, an ADDED (`+`) line matches\n   the EXISTING polyglot `_REMOVED_DECL_RE` (`registry.py:399-412` — Python `def`/`class`, Go\n   `func`, Rust `fn`, JS/TS `function`/arrow/`class`) and the NAME it declares is not also removed\n   on a `-` line in that same file (per-file provenance from the `diff --git … b/<path>` headers,\n   since the composed context interleaves files). `tests` is then selected only if NO changed file\n   matches the `tests` globs.\n   Added DECLARATIONS only. Branch-line (\"a new `if`/`for`\") detection is explicitly OUT — no cited\n   corpus case needs it; a follow-up may add it with its own case.\n3. Portable by construction, not by CI: an in-process pure-text scan, identical under the library,\n   CLI and remote-MCP harnesses and under any CI provider or none. It assumes NO language and NO\n   repository layout — no `src/**` predicate, no Python-only regex — so it fires for a Ruby, Java,\n   Next.js or .NET target as for this one. Its only path predicates are the `tests` globs\n   and a docs/data extension skip (`.md`, `.rst`, `.txt`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml`, `.toml`, `.cfg`,\n   `.ini`, `.lock`), so a fenced code block in a docs-only change cannot fire it.\n4. Name-not-text suppression is what the corpus requires: 1703 re-wraps signatures across lines, so\n   a line-TEXT comparison fails to suppress it but a NAME comparison succeeds. A MOVE is NOT\n   suppressed — the reviewed diff is `git diff base...head` with no `-M` (`assemble.py:230`), so a\n   rename arrives as delete-in-A + add-in-B whose added names have no removed counterpart; 1920 and\n   1737 trigger, by design.\n5. The scanned text is the COMPOSED context, not a raw diff: `overlay_union` receives\n   `steps.assemble_diff.outputs.context` (`gates/code-review.yaml:63`, `:116`) — a changed-files\n   list plus the diff truncated at `DIFF_CHAR_CAP = 60000` (`assemble.py:30`,\n   `compose_diff_context:77-92`). Both shapes are tested; a declaration past the cap does not\n   trigger (recorded blind spot), while `changed_files` is truncation-proof — hence keying the\n   rule's negative half on it.\n6. Narrow guard (vii) in `code-review-tests.md:97` so a coverage gap is blocking-eligible only when\n   the finding concerns *newly introduced behaviour* AND names a *violating input*. No trigger\n   provenance reaches the reviewer (`workflow_ops.py:61-65` supplies context/changed_files/\n   scope_context only), so the prompt DEFINES both from the diff alone: behaviour is *newly\n   introduced* when its implementing lines appear as ADDED (`+`) lines in the diff under review;\n   behaviour reachable only through unadded lines is *pre-existing* and stays advisory; a *named\n   violating input* is a concrete input value, argument or call sequence stated verbatim in the\n   finding that the added lines mishandle. ONE prompt serves Round-A and Round-B, so this also\n   changes blocking eligibility for the existing glob-triggered population (0.54, \"blocks 99\n   changes / 8.0%\") — intended, and the eval corpus gains the pre-existing-code FP case.\n\n## Scope\nUnder `src/rebar/llm/code_review/`: `registry.py` (594 lines, cap 800) — `changed_files` kwarg +\n`_has_added_declaration`; `workflow_ops.py` — pass `changed` at `:99` and refresh the step\n`description=` (`:70-86`), which names deletion-impact as the only content trigger;\n`criteria_routing.json` — provenance in the `tests` `_comment` only, `applies_to` unchanged.\nAlso `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md` (guard (vii)) and\n`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml` (one recall + one FP case, keeping\n`test_code_review_dataset_balanced` green); new `tests/unit/test_code_review_tests_trigger.py`\n(flat layout — `tests/unit/llm/` absent).\n\nAccepted: the `tests`-keyed Pass-4 coach moves (`moves.py:30`, `:75-82`) now offer on ordinary\nsource changes, and each qualifying change costs one extra uncapped Round-A overlay call (`cap: 3`\nis Round-B only, `code-review.yaml:120`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nUnless stated: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_tests_trigger.py -q`.\n- [ ] A diff whose only addition is a function/method/class declaration, with no changed test file,\n  selects `tests` from `content_triggered_overlays` and, through `overlay_union`, sets\n  `include_tests` true — asserted on BOTH a raw diff and its `compose_diff_context` output.\n- [ ] Parametrised replay over synthetic diffs of each cited shape: SELECT for `d9e0f0e733` (new\n  module, 15 added declarations), `721cb7d6ac` (moved declarations, 3), `1c2bf6e57b` (module split,\n  22); DO NOT SELECT for `24917e843b` (comment-only source delta — `git show 24917e843b -- 'src/*'\n  | grep -cE '^\\+\\s*(async +)?(def|class) '` returns `0`) and `83d91d488c` (annotation-only\n  rewrite; all 8 added names also removed in the same file).\n- [ ] Portability: an added declaration in a non-Python, non-`src/` file — a Go `func` under\n  `internal/`, a TS `export function` under `app/`, a Ruby `class` under `lib/` — selects `tests`,\n  while a docs-only diff whose markdown fence holds `def f():` and a config-only diff do NOT.\n- [ ] A test-file-only diff does not content-select it, and a diff adding a declaration *plus* a\n  `tests/` file still selects it by glob (union, not replacement).\n- [ ] Guard (vii) defines newly-introduced-vs-pre-existing behaviour and \"named violating input\" in\n  diff-decidable terms, with the Four-Criterion Test bullet unchanged; asserted via\n  `prompts.get_prompt(\"code-review-tests\")`.\n- [ ] No regression, no baseline edit: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_triggers.py\n  tests/unit/test_code_review_deletion_impact.py tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py\n  tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py -q` green with the first two unedited (35 tests),\n  `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` clean, and\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting `new=0 increased=0` with\n  `registry.py` under `.github/module-size-limit.txt`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787376834031940001,"uuid":"349f9ca1-0ffa-40c2-8919-b814350af01a"}